      "side": 1,
      "message": "No.  They are slightly different.\n\nchip_get_ec_int() accesses the hardware register to find out the INT number and saves to ec_int.\nintc_get_int() returns cached ec_int.\n\nNote that ec_int could be set by:  (see core/riscv-rv32i/task.c start_irq_handler())\n- chip_get_ec_int()\n- soft irq\n\nIn short, we cannot replace intc_get_ec_int() by chip_get_ec_int().\n\nHowever, we can remove intc_get_ec_int() since they can access the ec_int directly.\n\n\nI won\u0027t do that in this CL.  If you ask, I can submit another CL to remove intc_get_ec_int().",
      "parentUuid": "ce2f74f8_351a16d3",
      "range": {
